    {
      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n\n/* Packed entry for top-k list */\ntypedef struct {\n    float d;\n    char label;\n} Entry;\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    /* Count total points across all groups */\n    int total_points = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        total_points += groups[i].length;\n    }\n\n    /* Flatten point coordinates and labels into contiguous arrays */\n    float *xs = (float *)malloc(total_points * sizeof(float));\n    float *ys = (float *)malloc(total_points * sizeof(float));\n    char *labels_all = (char *)malloc(total_points * sizeof(char));\n\n    int idx = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            xs[idx] = g.points[j].x;\n            ys[idx] = g.points[j].y;\n            labels_all[idx] = g.label;\n            idx++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    /* Allocate top-k array of packed entries */\n    Entry *entries = (Entry *)malloc(k * sizeof(Entry));\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        entries[i].d = -1.0f;\n        entries[i].label = -1;\n    }\n\n    float qx = to_evaluate.x;\n    float qy = to_evaluate.y;\n\n    /* Main loop over all points (sequential access) */\n    for (int i = 0; i < total_points; i++) {\n        float dx = xs[i] - qx;\n        float dy = ys[i] - qy;\n        float d = dx*dx + dy*dy;\n\n        /* Insert into sorted top-k array */\n        for (int x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n            if (d < entries[x].d || entries[x].d == -1.0f) {\n                for (int y = k-1; y > x; y--) {\n                    entries[y] = entries[y-1];\n                }\n                entries[x].d = d;\n                entries[x].label = labels_all[i];\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    /* Extract labels for frequency counting */\n    char *labels = (char *)malloc(k * sizeof(char));\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = entries[i].label;\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    /* Find most frequent label */\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i-1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i-1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k-1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i-1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(xs);\n    free(ys);\n    free(labels_all);\n    free(entries);\n    free(labels);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Flattening all point coordinates into contiguous arrays (xs, ys) and packing distance-label pairs into a struct for the top-k list improves spatial locality. The main loop accesses memory sequentially instead of chasing pointers through separate Group structures and per-group malloc'd arrays; shifting packed entries reduces cache misses during insertion compared to maintaining two independent arrays.",
  "notes": "Only src/knn.c is modified. The algorithm logic (distance computation, sorted insertion, frequency counting) remains identical to the original. Memory for flattened arrays and top-k entries is freed after use.",
